<% content_for :title, "AI Product Leadership" %>
<% content_for :description, "I'm Aaron Grando, a Philadelphia-based product and technology leader. Explore the AI products I helped build at Mod Op and the decisions behind them." %>
        <div id="container">
            <section id="shield"><%= image_tag "shield.svg", width: 77, height: 97, alt: "Shield Emblem" %></section>
            <section id="bio">
                <h1>Aaron Grando</h1>
                <h2>I build AI products and lead the teams behind them.</h2>
                <p>
                    Hey, I'm Aaron. Most recently I was VP, Creative Innovation at Mod Op, where I led a six-person product and engineering team. We built the agency's shared AI platform and the products its client teams use on top of it.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    I came to product leadership through engineering and creative technology, and I still work that way. At Mod Op that meant writing the specs, working through architecture with the team, and building the first prototypes myself. Before that, fifteen years at a creative agency taught me how to explain new technology to clients and ship what they would use.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    I'm most at home where product strategy and platform architecture overlap: talking with people, deciding what to build, and staying close while the team builds it.
                </p>
                <p id="availability">
                    <span class="looking">I'm looking for my next full-time role in applied AI product leadership.</span>
                    <strong>Open to: </strong><br />VP / Head of Product &nbsp;·&nbsp; AI Product &amp; Platform &nbsp;·&nbsp; Creative&nbsp;Technology
                </p>
            </section>
            <section id="work" class="entries">
                <h3>Recent Work</h3>

                <p class="section-intro"><span class="company-label">Mod Op, 2024&ndash;2026.</span> I was a founding member of the Innovation team at Mod Op, a roughly 500-person agency, and led its first product engineering group. I owned six products in the AI portfolio from concept through launch, and helped shape the platform story that became Orion.</p>

                <p class="platform-feature">
                    <span class="feature-label">PLATFORM CASE STUDY</span>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/nexus">Orion and Nexus: the AI operating layer</a></strong>
                    Nexus gave the agency one place for company and client knowledge, with access rules that carried into its agents and its chat workspace. I led product and technical direction, starting with the accounts and configuration our first product needed and growing it as other teams needed the same things.
                    <br />
                    <span class="fun-fact"><strong>95% employee adoption · 700+ agents</strong> reported by Mod Op at Orion's July 2026 launch<br /><a href="https://digiday.com/marketing/build-or-buy-inside-indie-agency-mod-ops-ai-infrastructure/" target="_blank">Digiday put Orion's avoided licensing costs at roughly $3M</a> that August.</span>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/nexus#cs-context">Brand Agents</a></strong> AI assistants with a client's approved brand knowledge, voice, and goals already in place. I helped shape the product and <a href="https://www.modop.com/blog/brand-agent-how-we-created-ai-that-actually-helps-clients/" target="_blank">wrote its launch story</a>. In use since April 2025, with more than 200 client-specific agents deployed by August 2026.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/geo">GEO by Mod Op</a></strong> Shows a brand how it appears in AI-generated answers. I took it from a hackathon prototype to production with the agency's search and strategy teams, turning weekslong manual audits into a free automated audit and a paid program that pairs deeper analysis with the search team's work. Internal use began in June 2026 and Mod Op <a href="https://www.modop.com/press/mod-op-launches-free-ai-search-visibility-tool-and-unveils-the-geo-50/" target="_blank">launched it publicly</a> that August. <a href="https://geo.modop.ai" target="_blank">Try the free audit</a>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/launchpad">Launchpad</a></strong> I built Launchpad so our engineers could deploy prototypes without waiting on someone else to set up hosting, and shipped it the morning our first hackathon began. The cross-team sprints I organized in February and March 2026 produced more than 60 working prototypes. Launchpad also gave colleagues an internal directory where they could try the work and leave feedback.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/mod-heat">Mod Heat</a></strong> Finds the news and cultural moments relevant to a client, then uses Brand Agents to generate ideas for how the brand could respond. I originated the concept, pitched it to the executive team, and shipped it with my team in November 2024 as Mod Op Innovation&rsquo;s first product release.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Audience Lab</strong> Audience simulations for creative pretesting, built from customer and buyer data as digital twins. I started prototyping it in 2023, before Mod Op acquired RTO+P, and directed the production release in May 2026, which uses <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.08338" target="_blank">Semantic Similarity Rating</a>. I onboarded the strategists who now run it in client-facing creative development.
                </p>
            </section>
